## Why This Is Asked
Real-world federated privacy requires strict budget governance and data locality to satisfy regional compliance and tenant SLAs, while still enabling global analytics.

## Key Concepts
- Differential privacy budgets per tenant and per region
- Data locality constraints and secure regional processing
- Auditable, tamper-evident logs and rollback paths
- Lightweight per-tenant APIs for budget, policy, and audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple DP budget ledger update (conceptual)
function adjustBudget(tenant, epsDelta, deltaNotes){
  const rec = getBudget(tenant);
  rec.epsilon += epsDelta;
  rec.delta += deltaNotes?.delta || 0;
  saveBudget(tenant, rec);
  return rec;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for late-joining tenants violating region policy?
- How would you handle key rotation and audit-log integrity across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Observability and data quality are foundational for reliable analytics. This question probes practical patterns a junior engineer can implement end-to-end, including validation, DLQ routing, metrics, and watermarking.

## Key Concepts
- Schema validation at ingestion
- Dead-letter queue for bad data
- Per-field quality metrics
- Watermarks and late data handling
- Lightweight testing with synthetic data

## Code Example
```javascript
function validateEvent(e) {
  if (!e) return false;
  const fields = ['user_id','event_type','ts','event_id'];
  for (const f of fields) if (!(f in e)) return false;
  const ts = Number(new Date(e.ts));
  if (Number.isNaN(ts) || ts < 0) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate DLQ integrity under burst loads?
- How would you extend to schema evolution without breaking dashboards?

